## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a concrete, end-to-end data pipeline that combines simple AI tasks with serverless orchestration. It emphasizes data validation, privacy controls, and cost awareness at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven Lambda triggered by S3
- JSON schema validation in Lambda
- Amazon Comprehend: sentiment and entity detection
- S3 write of analysis artifacts
- DynamoDB upsert for indexing
- IAM least-privilege principles and KMS encryption
- Basic error handling with DLQ and monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda: pseudo Skeleton
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  // 1) get object from S3
  // 2) validate with JSON Schema
  // 3) run Comprehend DetectSentiment and DetectEntities on feedback
  // 4) write analysis JSON to S3
  // 5) upsert DynamoDB with bundleId, s3Key, sentiment, entities
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema drift over time?
- What tests would you add to verify end-to-end correctness and cost limits?

